{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794755475,"nonce":"tvVhw6FJ/OzRkVGPh+rdZQDNSio=","title":"CSS transitions that rows cannot carry are still painted in full every frame","message":"What d135320b carries is a transition of transform (uniform scale) or of opacity on a node that paints one filled rectangle, with nothing else changing. The rest keep the path they had, which is a full paint every frame where the subtree cannot be a texture:\n\n- a transition that changes a colour, a border, a shadow or a radius along with, or instead of, the transform. Most cn hover transitions are these (background, border-color); they need paint tracks (54771c4).\n- opacity on a node that paints more than one draw, or has children: a bound opacity is a group (82cb190).\n- a node with a `transform-origin`, a transition that stretches one axis alone or shears.\n- a transition running on a node that also has a CSS animation.\n\nEach of these falls back by returning `None` from `css_transition_delta` in blinc_layout's css animation module, so the cases are one place. Measure before choosing: what_a_css_transition_frame_costs in blinc_recorder's animation_paths.\n\nLabels: perf, area:layout, area:animation.","files":null}]}